    "summary": "Slip catalogue:\r\nGlazed pottery jar with square base and circular neck. The greatest breadth is reached at about the centre of the jar where the round neck meets the rectangular body. The surface is ornamented with rectangular and rhomboidal yellow fields on which are hatched lozenges, triangles etc and which are bordered with black. The interspaces between these fields are dull red, and ornamented with circular yellow spots.",
